&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id=&#34;circuit-breaker&#34;&gt;Circuit Breaker&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;circuit-breaker&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#circuit-breaker&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fuse connection between Apache ShardingSphere and the database.
When an Apache ShardingSphere node exceeds the max load, stop the node&amp;rsquo;s access to the database,
so that the database can ensure sufficient resources to provide services for other Apache ShardingSphere nodes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id=&#34;request-limit&#34;&gt;Request Limit&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;request-limit&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#request-limit&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;In the face of overload requests, open request limiting to protect some requests can still respond quickly.&lt;/p&gt;

      </description>
